* prism.def: the Prism3D engine device. Add it to any SIPL script the engine runs. *
* Units: positions and scales in thousandths (1000 = 1.0), angles in thousandths of a degree, *
* times in milliseconds, colours as 0xRRGGBB. The world is right-handed, +Y up, cameras look down -Z. *
port prism.frame (write)        * doorbell: end this frame; the script resumes next frame *
port prism.quit (read)          * 1 once the window was closed *
port prism.ms (read)            * milliseconds since the engine started *
port prism.dt (read)            * milliseconds the last frame took *
port prism.tier (read)          * render tier: 0 software, 1 fixed-function, 2 shaders, 3 modern *
port prism.self (read)          * id of the object this script is attached to *
port prism.sel (read, write)    * the selected object id; the transform and look registers act on it *
port prism.spawn (write)        * create a primitive (1 cube, 2 sphere, 3 plane) and select it *
port prism.camera (write)       * create a camera (write 1 to also make it the active one) and select it *
port prism.light (write)        * create a light (0 directional, 1 point) and select it *
port prism.destroy (write)      * destroy an object by id *
port prism.active (write)       * make object id the active camera *
port prism.px (read, write)
port prism.py (read, write)
port prism.pz (read, write)
port prism.rx (read, write)
port prism.ry (read, write)
port prism.rz (read, write)
port prism.sx (read, write)
port prism.sy (read, write)
port prism.sz (read, write)
port prism.color (read, write)  * mesh colour, or a light's colour *
port prism.shade (write)        * 0 unlit, 1 flat, 2 per vertex, 3 per pixel; falls back per tier *
port prism.tex (write)          * texture id: 0 none, 1 built-in checker, or from prism.texload *
port prism.texload (write, str) * load an image file; its id is then in prism.texid (0 = failed) *
port prism.texid (read)
port prism.range (read, write)  * point light range *
port prism.clear (write)        * background colour *
port prism.ambient (write)      * ambient light colour *
port prism.mousex (read)
port prism.mousey (read)
port prism.buttons (read)       * bit 0 left, bit 1 middle, bit 2 right *
port prism.log (write, str)     * print a line to the engine log *
mem prism.keys (length 512, flag R) * one byte per key (USB HID usage / SDL scancode), 1 = held *
